# Always Use Tailwind Notifications

For **in-app user feedback** (success, error, warning, info), use the Tailwind toast system. Do not use `alert()`, `confirm()` for simple messages, or ad-hoc DOM toasts.

## API

- **In Vue components / composables:** `useNotifications()` from `@/composables/useNotifications`
- **Outside setup / after unmount:** `showGlobalNotification(message, options)` from the same module

`NotificationContainer` + `ToastNotificationCard` render top-right Tailwind toasts. Helpdesk realtime alerts use structured fields (icon, category, primary, secondary, meta) via `showHelpdeskNotificationToast()` / `buildHelpdeskToastPresentation()`.

```js
import { useNotifications } from '@/composables/useNotifications';

const { success, error, warning, info } = useNotifications();

success(t('records.genericEmailSent'));
error(err?.response?.data?.message || t('records.genericEmailSendFailed'));
warning(t('common.sessionChanged'), 6000);
```

```js
import { showGlobalNotification } from '@/composables/useNotifications';

import { showHelpdeskNotificationToast } from '@/utils/notificationToast';

showHelpdeskNotificationToast(notification, { appKey: 'HELPDESK', playSound: true });
```

## Clickable helpdesk toasts

Pass `appKey`, `entity`, and `notificationId` so `NotificationContainer` can open the related record tab on click (see `helpdeskNotificationAlerts.js`).

## What not to use for in-app feedback

| Avoid | Use instead |
|-------|-------------|
| `alert('Saved')` | `success(...)` |
| `alert(err.message)` | `error(...)` |
| Custom floating divs | `useNotifications()` |
| `console.log` as user feedback | Toast helpers |

## Exceptions (not in-app toasts)

- **Browser push:** `Notification.requestPermission()`, `registration.showNotification()`, and `new Notification()` are for OS-level push tests and background delivery — keep those in notification settings / push subscription flows only.
- **`confirm()`** for destructive actions is still acceptable when a modal is not used yet.

When touching files that still use `alert()` for feedback, migrate them to `useNotifications()` in the same change.
